 The environment variable `VLLM_ALLOW_LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN=1` is required at the moment.","ordered":false,"start":"","loose":false,"items":[{"type":"list_item","raw":"- The environment variable `VLLM_ALLOW_LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN=1` is required at the moment.","task":false,"loose":false,"text":"The environment variable `VLLM_ALLOW_LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN=1` is required at the moment.","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"The environment variable `VLLM_ALLOW_LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN=1` is required at the moment.","text":"The environment variable `VLLM_ALLOW_LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN=1` is required at the moment.","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"The environment variable ","text":"The environment variable ","escaped":false},{"type":"codespan","raw":"`VLLM_ALLOW_LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN=1`","text":"VLLM_ALLOW_LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN=1"},{"type":"text","raw":" is required at the moment.","text":" is required at the moment.","escaped":false}]}]}]}],"text":"**Note**\n- The environment variable `VLLM_ALLOW_LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN=1` is required at the moment."},{"type":"space","raw":"\n\n"},{"type":"blockquote","raw":"> **Note**\n> - The default context length is 256K. Consider reducing the context length to a smaller value, e.g., `32768`, if the server fail to start.","tokens":[{"type":"paragraph","raw":"**Note**\n","text":"**Note**","tokens":[{"type":"strong","raw":"**Note**","text":"Note","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"Note","text":"Note","escaped":false}]}]},{"type":"list","raw":"- The default context length is 256K. Consider reducing the context length to a smaller value, e.g., `32768`, if the server fail to start.","ordered":false,"start":"","loose":false,"items":[{"type":"list_item","raw":"- The default context length is 256K. Consider reducing the context length to a smaller value, e.g., `32768`, if the server fail to start.","task":false,"loose":false,"text":"The default context length is 256K. Consider reducing the context length to a smaller value, e.g., `32768`, if the server fail to start.","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"The default context length is 256K. Consider reducing the context length to a smaller value, e.g., `32768`, if the server fail to start.","text":"The default context length is 256K. Consider reducing the context length to a smaller value, e.g., `32768`, if the server fail to start.","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"The default context length is 256K. Consider reducing the context length to a smaller value, e.g., ","text":"The default context length is 256K. Consider reducing the context length to a smaller value, e.g., ","escaped":false},{"type":"codespan","raw":"`32768`","text":"32768"},{"type":"text","raw":", if the server fail to start.","text":", if the server fail to start.","escaped":false}]}]}]}],"text":"**Note**\n- The default context length is 256K. Consider reducing the context length to a smaller value, e.g., `32768`, if the server fail to start."},{"type":"space","raw":"\n\n"},{"type":"heading","raw":"### Agentic Use\n\n","depth":3,"text":"Agentic Use","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"Agentic Use","text":"Agentic Use","escaped":false}]},{"type":"paragraph","raw":"Qwen3 excels in tool calling capabilities. We recommend using [Qwen-Agent](https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen-Agent) to make the best use of agentic ability of Qwen3. Qwen-Agent encapsulates tool-calling templates and tool-calling parsers internally, greatly reducing coding complexity.","text":"Qwen3 excels in tool calling capabilities. We recommend using [Qwen-Agent](https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen-Agent) to make the best use of agentic ability of Qwen3. Qwen-Agent encapsulates tool-calling templates and tool-calling parsers internally, greatly reducing coding complexity.","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"Qwen3 excels in tool calling capabilities. We recommend using ","text":"Qwen3 excels in tool calling capabilities. We recommend using ","escaped":false},{"type":"link","raw":"[Qwen-Agent](https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen-Agent)","href":"https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen-Agent","title":null,"text":"Qwen-Agent","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"Qwen-Agent","text":"Qwen-Agent","escaped":false}]},{"type":"text","raw":" to make the best use of agentic ability of Qwen3. Qwen-Agent encapsulates tool-calling templates and tool-calling parsers internally, greatly reducing coding complexity.","text":" to make the best use of agentic ability of Qwen3. Qwen-Agent encapsulates tool-calling templates and tool-calling parsers internally, greatly reducing coding complexity.","escaped":false}]},{"type":"space","raw":"\n\n"},{"type":"paragraph","raw":"To define the available tools, you can use the MCP configuration file, use the integrated tool of Qwen-Agent, or integrate other tools by yourself.","text":"To define the available tools, you can use the MCP configuration file, use the integrated tool of Qwen-Agent, or integrate other tools by yourself.","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"To define the available tools, you can use the MCP configuration file, use the integrated tool of Qwen-Agent, or integrate other tools by yourself.","text":"To define the available tools, you can use the MCP configuration file, use the integrated tool of Qwen-Agent, or integrate other tools by yourself.","escaped":false}]},{"type":"code","name":"code","src":"https://docs.qwenlm.ai/research/qwen3-next/code/6184c986-8ad7-40e3-b043-606797b3c75c.py","lang":"python","attributes":{},"raw":"{{< code src=\"./code/6184c986-8ad7-40e3-b043-606797b3c75c.py\" lang=\"python\" >}}","tokens":[]},{"type":"paragraph","raw":"}}","text":"}}","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"}}","text":"}}","escaped":false}]},{"type":"space","raw":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"heading","raw":"### Processing Ultra-Long Texts\n\n","depth":3,"text":"Processing Ultra-Long Texts","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"Processing Ultra-Long Texts","text":"Processing Ultra-Long Texts","escaped":false}]},{"type":"paragraph","raw":"Qwen3-Next natively supports context lengths of up to 262,144 tokens. For conversations where the total length (including both input and output) significantly exceeds this limit, we recommend using RoPE scaling techniques to handle long texts effectively. We have validated the model's performance on context lengths of up to 1 million tokens using the [YaRN](https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.00071) method.","text":"Qwen3-Next natively supports context lengths of up to 262,144 tokens. For conversations where the total length (including both input and output) significantly exceeds this limit, we recommend using RoPE scaling techniques to handle long texts effectively. We have validated the model's performance on context lengths of up to 1 million tokens using the [YaRN](https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.00071) method.","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"Qwen3-Next natively supports context lengths of up to 262,144 tokens. For conversations where the total length (including both input and output) significantly exceeds this limit, we recommend using RoPE scaling techniques to handle long texts effectively. We have validated the model's performance on context lengths of up to 1 million tokens using the ","text":"Qwen3-Next natively supports context lengths of up to 262,144 tokens. For conversations where the total length (including both input and output) significantly exceeds this limit, we recommend using RoPE scaling techniques to handle long texts effectively. We have validated the model's performance on context lengths of up to 1 million tokens using the ","escaped":false},{"type":"link","raw":"[YaRN](https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.00071)","href":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.00071","title":null,"text":"YaRN","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"YaRN","text":"YaRN","escaped":false}]},{"type":"text","raw":" method.","text":" method.","escaped":false}]},{"type":"space","raw":"\n\n"},{"type":"paragraph","raw":"YaRN is currently supported by several inference frameworks, e.g., `transformers`, `vllm` and `sglang`. In general, there are two approaches to enabling YaRN for supported frameworks:","text":"YaRN is currently supported by several inference frameworks, e.g., `transformers`, `vllm` and `sglang`. In general, there are two approaches to enabling YaRN for supported frameworks:","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"YaRN is currently supported by several inference frameworks, e.g., ","text":"YaRN is currently supported by several inference frameworks, e.g., ","escaped":false},{"type":"codespan","raw":"`transformers`","text":"transformers"},{"type":"text","raw":", ","text":", ","escaped":false},{"type":"codespan","raw":"`vllm`","text":"vllm"},{"type":"text","raw":" and ","text":" and ","escaped":false},{"type":"codespan","raw":"`sglang`","text":"sglang"},{"type":"text","raw":". In general, there are two approaches to enabling YaRN for supported frameworks:","text":". In general, there are two approaches to enabling YaRN for supported frameworks:","escaped":false}]},{"type":"space","raw":"\n\n"},{"type":"list","raw":"- Modifying the model files:\n  In the `config.json` file, add the `rope_scaling` fields:\n\n    {{< code src=\"./code/c1e7f2f6-217e-4a2b-ae2b-3f528ae5584d.json\" lang=\"json\" >}}\n\n- Passing command line arguments:\n\n  For `vllm`, you can use\n\n    {{< code src=\"./code/29ae8b64-7483-436c-8095-a5acabfa7393.sh\" lang=\"shell\" >}}\n\n  For `sglang`, you can use\n\n    {{< code src=\"./code/9e4b5c14-057a-46a4-bf72-946d6785a247.sh\" lang=\"shell\" >}}","ordered":false,"start":"","loose":true,"items":[{"type":"list_item","raw":"- Modifying the model files:\n  In the `config.json` file, add the `rope_scaling` fields:\n\n    {{< code src=\"./code/c1e7f2f6-217e-4a2b-ae2b-3f528ae5584d.json\" lang=\"json\" >}}\n\n","task":false,"loose":true,"text":"Modifying the model files:\nIn the `config.json` file, add the `rope_scaling` fields:\n\n  {{< code src=\"./code/c1e7f2f6-217e-4a2b-ae2b-3f528ae5584d.json\" lang=\"json\" >}}\n","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"Modifying the model files:\n\nIn the `config.json` file, add the `rope_scaling` fields:","text":"Modifying the model files:\nIn the `config.json` file, add the `rope_scaling` fields:","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"Modifying the model files:","text":"Modifying the model files:","escaped":false},{"type":"br","raw":"\n"},{"type":"text","raw":"In the ","text":"In the ","escaped":false},{"type":"codespan","raw":"`config.json`","text":"config.json"},{"type":"text","raw":" file, add the ","text":" file, add the ","escaped":false},{"type":"codespan","raw":"`rope_scaling`","text":"rope_scaling"},{"type":"text","raw":" fields:","text":" fields:","escaped":false}]},{"type":"code","name":"code","src":"https://docs.qwenlm.ai/research/qwen3-next/code/c1e7f2f6-217e-4a2b-ae2b-3f528ae5584d.json","lang":"json","attributes":{},"raw":"{{< code src=\"./code/c1e7f2f6-217e-4a2b-ae2b-3f528ae5584d.json\" lang=\"json\" >}}","tokens":[]},{"type":"blockquote","raw":" >}}\n","tokens":[{"type":"paragraph","raw":"}}","text":"}}","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"}}","text":"}}","escaped":false}]}],"text":"}}"}]},{"type":"list_item","raw":"- Passing command line arguments:\n\n  For `vllm`, you can use\n\n    {{< code src=\"./code/29ae8b64-7483-436c-8095-a5acabfa7393.sh\" lang=\"shell\" >}}\n\n  For `sglang`, you can use\n\n    {{< code src=\"./code/9e4b5c14-057a-46a4-bf72-946d6785a247.sh\" lang=\"shell\" >}}","task":false,"loose":true,"text":"Passing command line arguments:\n\nFor `vllm`, you can use\n\n  {{< code src=\"./code/29ae8b64-7483-436c-8095-a5acabfa7393.sh\" lang=\"shell\" >}}\n\nFor `sglang`, you can use\n\n  {{< code src=\"./code/9e4b5c14-057a-46a4-bf72-946d6785a247.sh\" lang=\"shell\" >}}","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"Passing command line arguments:","text":"Passing command line arguments:","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"Passing command line arguments:","text":"Passing command line arguments:","escaped":false}]},{"type":"space","raw":"\n\n"},{"type":"text","raw":"For `vllm`, you can use","text":"For `vllm`, you can use","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"For ","text":"For ","escaped":false},{"type":"codespan","raw":"`vllm`","text":"vllm"},{"type":"text","raw":", you can use","text":", you can use","escaped":false}]},{"type":"code","name":"code","src":"https://docs.qwenlm.ai/research/qwen3-next/code/29ae8b64-7483-436c-8095-a5acabfa7393.sh","lang":"shell","attributes":{},"raw":"{{< code src=\"./code/29ae8b64-7483-436c-8095-a5acabfa7393.sh\" lang=\"shell\" >}}","tokens":[]},{"type":"blockquote","raw":" >}}","tokens":[{"type":"paragraph","raw":"}}","text":"}}","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"}}","text":"}}","escaped":false}]}],"text":"}}"},{"type":"space","raw":"\n\n"},{"type":"text","raw":"For `sglang`, you can use","text":"For `sglang`, you can use","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"For ","text":"For ","escaped":false},{"type":"codespan","raw":"`sglang`","text":"sglang"},{"type":"text","raw":", you can use","text":", you can use","escaped":false}]},{"type":"code","name":"code","src":"https://docs.qwenlm.ai/research/qwen3-next/code/9e4b5c14-057a-46a4-bf72-946d6785a247.sh","lang":"shell","attributes":{},"raw":"{{< code src=\"./code/9e4b5c14-057a-46a4-bf72-946d6785a247.sh\" lang=\"shell\" >}}","tokens":[]},{"type":"blockquote","raw":" >}}","tokens":[{"type":"paragraph","raw":"}}","text":"}}","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"}}","text":"}}","escaped":false}]}],"text":"}}"}]}]},{"type":"space","raw":"\n\n"},{"type":"blockquote","raw":"> **NOTE**:\n> - All the notable open-source frameworks implement static YaRN, which means the scaling factor remains constant regardless of input length, **potentially impacting performance on shorter texts.**\n> - We advise adding the `rope_scaling` configuration only when processing long contexts is required. \n> - It is also recommended to modify the `factor` as needed. For example, if the typical context length for your application is 524,288 tokens, it would be better to set `factor` as 2.0. ","tokens":[{"type":"paragraph","raw":"**NOTE**:\n","text":"**NOTE**:","tokens":[{"type":"strong","raw":"**NOTE**","text":"NOTE","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"NOTE","text":"NOTE","escaped":false}]},{"type":"text","raw":":","text":":","escaped":false}]},{"type":"list","raw":"- All the notable open-source frameworks implement static YaRN, which means the scaling factor remains constant regardless of input length, **potentially impacting performance on shorter texts.**\n- We advise adding the `rope_scaling` configuration only when processing long contexts is required. \n- It is also recommended to modify the `factor` as needed. For example, if the typical context length for your application is 524,288 tokens, it would be better to set `factor` as 2.0.\n","ordered":false,"start":"","loose":false,"items":[{"type":"list_item","raw":"- All the notable open-source frameworks implement static YaRN, which means the scaling factor remains constant regardless of input length, **potentially impacting performance on shorter texts.**\n","task":false,"loose":false,"text":"All the notable open-source frameworks implement static YaRN, which means the scaling factor remains constant regardless of input length, **potentially impacting performance on shorter texts.**","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"All the notable open-source frameworks implement static YaRN, which means the scaling factor remains constant regardless of input length, **potentially impacting performance on shorter texts.**","text":"All the notable open-source frameworks implement static YaRN, which means the scaling factor remains constant regardless of input length, **potentially impacting performance on shorter texts.**","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"All the notable open-source frameworks implement static YaRN, which means the scaling factor remains constant regardless of input length, ","text":"All the notable open-source frameworks implement static YaRN, which means the scaling factor remains constant regardless of input length, ","escaped":false},{"type":"strong","raw":"**potentially impacting performance on shorter texts.**","text":"potentially impacting performance on shorter texts.","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"potentially impacting performance on shorter texts.","text":"potentially impacting performance on shorter texts.","escaped":false}]}]}]},{"type":"list_item","raw":"- We advise adding the `rope_scaling` configuration only when processing long contexts is required. \n","task":false,"loose":false,"text":"We advise adding the `rope_scaling` configuration only when processing long contexts is required. ","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"We advise adding the `rope_scaling` configuration only when processing long contexts is required. ","text":"We advise adding the `rope_scaling` configuration only when processing long contexts is required. ","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"We advise adding the ","text":"We advise adding the ","escaped":false},{"type":"codespan","raw":"`rope_scaling`","text":"rope_scaling"},{"type":"text","raw":" configuration only when processing long contexts is required. ","text":" configuration only when processing long contexts is required. ","escaped":false}]}]},{"type":"list_item","raw":"- It is also recommended to modify the `factor` as needed. For example, if the typical context length for your application is 524,288 tokens, it would be better to set `factor` as 2.0.","task":false,"loose":false,"text":"It is also recommended to modify the `factor` as needed. For example, if the typical context length for your application is 524,288 tokens, it would be better to set `factor` as 2.0.","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"It is also recommended to modify the `factor` as needed. For example, if the typical context length for your application is 524,288 tokens, it would be better to set `factor` as 2.0.","text":"It is also recommended to modify the `factor` as needed. For example, if the typical context length for your application is 524,288 tokens, it would be better to set `factor` as 2.0.","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"It is also recommended to modify the ","text":"It is also recommended to modify the ","escaped":false},{"type":"codespan","raw":"`factor`","text":"factor"},{"type":"text","raw":" as needed. For example, if the typical context length for your application is 524,288 tokens, it would be better to set ","text":" as needed. For example, if the typical context length for your application is 524,288 tokens, it would be better to set ","escaped":false},{"type":"codespan","raw":"`factor`","text":"factor"},{"type":"text","raw":" as 2.0.","text":" as 2.0.","escaped":false}]}]}]}],"text":"**NOTE**:\n- All the notable open-source frameworks implement static YaRN, which means the scaling factor remains constant regardless of input length, **potentially impacting performance on shorter texts.**\n- We advise adding the `rope_scaling` configuration only when processing long contexts is required. \n- It is also recommended to modify the `factor` as needed. For example, if the typical context length for your application is 524,288 tokens, it would be better to set `factor` as 2.0. "},{"type":"space","raw":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"heading","raw":"## Summary\n\n","depth":2,"text":"Summary","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"Summary","text":"Summary","escaped":false}]},{"type":"paragraph","raw":"Qwen3-Next represents a major leap forward in model architecture, introducing innovations in attention mechanisms, including linear attention and attention gate, as well as increased sparsity in its MoE design. Qwen3-Next-80B-A3B delivers performance on par with the larger Qwen3-235B-A22B-2507 across both thinking and non-thinking modes, while offering significantly faster inference, especially in long-context scenarios. With this release, we aim to empower the open-source community to evolve alongside cutting-edge architectural advances. Looking ahead, we will further refine this architecture to develop Qwen3.5, targeting unprecedented levels of intelligence and productivity.","text":"Qwen3-Next represents a major leap forward in model architecture, introducing innovations in attention mechanisms, including linear attention and attention gate, as well as increased sparsity in its MoE design. Qwen3-Next-80B-A3B delivers performance on par with the larger Qwen3-235B-A22B-2507 across both thinking and non-thinking modes, while offering significantly faster inference, especially in long-context scenarios. With this release, we aim to empower the open-source community to evolve alongside cutting-edge architectural advances. Looking ahead, we will further refine this architecture to develop Qwen3.5, targeting unprecedented levels of intelligence and productivity.","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"Qwen3-Next represents a major leap forward in model architecture, introducing innovations in attention mechanisms, including linear attention and attention gate, as well as increased sparsity in its MoE design. Qwen3-Next-80B-A3B delivers performance on par with the larger Qwen3-235B-A22B-2507 across both thinking and non-thinking modes, while offering significantly faster inference, especially in long-context scenarios. With this release, we aim to empower the open-source community to evolve alongside cutting-edge architectural advances. Looking ahead, we will further refine this architecture to develop Qwen3.5, targeting unprecedented levels of intelligence and productivity.","text":"Qwen3-Next represents a major leap forward in model architecture, introducing innovations in attention mechanisms, including linear attention and attention gate, as well as increased sparsity in its MoE design. Qwen3-Next-80B-A3B delivers performance on par with the larger Qwen3-235B-A22B-2507 across both thinking and non-thinking modes, while offering significantly faster inference, especially in long-context scenarios. With this release, we aim to empower the open-source community to evolve alongside cutting-edge architectural advances. Looking ahead, we will further refine this architecture to develop Qwen3.5, targeting unprecedented levels of intelligence and productivity.","escaped":false}]},{"type":"space","raw":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"heading","raw":"# References\n\n","depth":1,"text":"References","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"References","text":"References","escaped":false}]},{"type":"hr"},{"type":"footnote","raw":"[^1]: Gated Delta Networks: Improving Mamba2 with Delta Rule\n\n","label":"1","refs":[],"content":[{"type":"space","raw":"\n"},{"type":"paragraph","raw":"Gated Delta Networks: Improving Mamba2 with Delta Rule\n","text":"Gated Delta Networks: Improving Mamba2 with Delta Rule","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"Gated Delta Networks: Improving Mamba2 with Delta Rule","text":"Gated Delta Networks: Improving Mamba2 with Delta Rule","escaped":false}]}]},{"type":"footnote","raw":"[^2]: Gated Attention for Large Language Models: Non-linearity, Sparsity, and Attention-Sink-Free\n\n","label":"2","refs":[],"content":[{"type":"space","raw":"\n"},{"type":"paragraph","raw":"Gated Attention for Large Language Models: Non-linearity, Sparsity, and Attention-Sink-Free\n","text":"Gated Attention for Large Language Models: Non-linearity, Sparsity, and Attention-Sink-Free","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"Gated Attention for Large Language Models: Non-linearity, Sparsity, and Attention-Sink-Free","text":"Gated Attention for Large Language Models: Non-linearity, Sparsity, and Attention-Sink-Free","escaped":false}]}]},{"type":"footnote","raw":"[^3]: DeepSeek-V3 Technical Report\n\n","label":"3","refs":[],"content":[{"type":"space","raw":"\n"},{"type":"paragraph","raw":"DeepSeek-V3 Technical Report\n","text":"DeepSeek-V3 Technical Report","tokens":[{"type":"text","raw":"DeepSeek-V3 Technical Report","text":"DeepSeek-V3 Technical Report","escaped":false}]}]},{"type":"footnote","raw":"[^4]: Demons in the Detail: On Implementing Load Balancing Loss for Training Specialized Mixture-of-Expert Models\n\n","label":"4","refs":[],"content":[{"type":"space","raw":"\n"},{"type":"paragraph","raw":"Demons in the Detail: On Implementing Load Balancing Loss for